  "502": {
    "inputs": {
      "label_json": "{\"text\":\"1. Turn Seamless Video Continuation & Single Pass ON in the Options.\\n2. Load your video in the Video 1 slot and click the yellow Scissors icon.\\n  - the left side (beginning) is where your video will start after being stitched together.\\n  - the right side (end) is where your gen will continue from.\\n   (IDEALLY your video is 24 FPS and already the correct size/aspect ratio\\n   as mismatched video can result in imperfect continuations! Use Crop tool to resize.)\\n3. Select Overlap Frames (5, 22, 39, or 56). This is the # of frames Minimax\\n     has access to as reference for how to continue your video.\\n4. If your video has no audio, turn on the OG Vid Has No Audio option to the right.\\n5. Since this is Single Pass, change your video genning settings:\\n   - Steps: 6-10+\\n   - Increase megapixels (since there will be no upscaling, higher is better).\\n   - Turn off Previews #2 and #3\\n   - Turn off Final Upscale Pass\\n6. Prompt! Remember that the first X Overlap frames of your gen are SPOKEN FOR!\\n   In order to get seamless continuation, start with\\n   \\\"a single continuous shot from beginning to end\\\" and then describe what's happening\\n   in a way that the model will understand how it can continue the shot.\\n\\nSeamless Video Continuation is for changing existing videos, and for creating\\nsingle-take shots longer than 15s. It is not a replacement for video editing, and if you \\ncan get away with cuts then just use normal genning practices with references to your \\nprevious shots/scenes.\\\\n\\\\nThe more overlap frames, the slower the gen (go figure).\",\"fontSize\":14,\"fontFamily\":\"Arial\",\"fontColor\":\"#000000\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#ffd166\",\"padding\":10,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaLabel",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Label Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "503": {
    "inputs": {
      "label_json": "{\"text\":\"If you get: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'shape' error - Turn Single Pass ON! You forgot.\",\"fontSize\":18,\"fontFamily\":\"Arial\",\"fontColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#f66744\",\"padding\":10,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaLabel",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Label Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "504": {
    "inputs": {
      "label_json": "{\"text\":\"Workflow will finalize Preview #1 (No Upscale). Turn off Previews #2, #3, and Upscale Pass.\\nBest at 1.0-2.0 MP, 6-10 steps w/ Turbo. Note: Single Pass is required for Video Continuation.\",\"fontSize\":10,\"fontFamily\":\"Arial\",\"fontColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#ff8c42\",\"padding\":7,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaLabel",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Label Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "507": {
    "inputs": {
      "label_json": "{\"text\":\"^ must be a multiple of (17n+5) like 5, 22, 39, 56...\\notherwise you get ghosting\",\"fontSize\":10,\"fontFamily\":\"Arial\",\"fontColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#333333\",\"padding\":7,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaLabel",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Label Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "508": {
    "inputs": {
      "label_json": "{\"text\":\"Start your upscale by clicking Run or the button below.\\nIf you don't like the result, you can reroll by clicking Manual Random Seed\\nas many times as you like to get variations of the first pass! \\n(Unless\\nyou change something like prompt, resolution, refs, ANYTHING\\nthat happened before this step, which will force Stage 1 to regen.)\\n(If Stage 1 always regens even if you didn't change anything, make sure\\nyour comfy startup isn't using --no-cache)\",\"fontSize\":14,\"fontFamily\":\"Arial\",\"fontColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#333333\",\"padding\":10,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"
    },
