  "549": {
    "inputs": {
      "label_json": "{\"text\":\"Using the Audio Voice Cloner:\\n1. Switch it on / Make sure Previews 1-3 are on / Turn Final Upscale Pass off.\\n2. By default, it uses whatever's loaded in the \\\"Custom Voice Reference\\\" Audio Loader.\\n   Toggle \\\"Use Custom Voice Reference\\\" OFF to use whatever is loaded into <Audio 1> in the main Ref Loader. \\n   If no audio is loaded in <Audio 1> and \\\"Use Custom Voice Reference\\\" is off, the voice will be fully AI generated.\\n   You can describe the qualities of their voice in the \\\"Tone\\\" text field.\\n3. Write your line of dialogue.\\n4. Chose your Tone, the format should be \\\"her tone is...\\\" and proceed from there.\\n  This is generally where you'd write any line delivery details, inflections, specifics. Can be blank if neutral.\\n5. Set audio gen length -- Too high and the character babbles to fill the time, too low and they speedrun the line.\\n  You have to estimate how long it takes to say the line of dialogue at the pace you want.\\n6. Gen! The files all get saved to output/seedhunter_audio/\\n\\n------\\nUseful tips:\\n- Use *asterisks* to emphasize words in dialogue: \\\"I like *YOUR* muffins, not *HIS*.\\\"\\n- Change your quality to the HIGHest setting if you need to squeeze more emotional width out of the character.\\n- 16 steps/simple is the best preset I could find so far to balance quality vs. speed.\\n- Tonal delivery can have a lot of information in it, such as how a character says specific words. Experiment!\\n- You can tweak the template prompt to fine tune even further.\",\"fontSize\":14,\"fontFamily\":\"Arial\",\"fontColor\":\"#ffffff\",\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#543a69\",\"padding\":10,\"borderRadius\":6,\"opacity\":1,\"fontWeight\":\"normal\",\"lineHeight\":1}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaLabel",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Label Pixaroma"
    }
  },
